{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"creatable-foldable-arthropods","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem / authority\n\nThe completion-verification close gate still fails to close **legitimately complete** tickets,\npushing authors to `--force`, because the verifier agent loops on repeated file reads. This is\nthe exact user-visible symptom that bug `brusque-tippable-sunbittern` (46a2-9c1a-d855-4706)\nnamed as its goal to eliminate: \"a legitimately complete ticket cannot be closed through the\ngate ... an infrastructure loop silently pushes authors toward bypassing a safety gate.\"\n\nWhat shipped for that bug (consolidated into epic `9b71-55b3-1bd1-4a97`, live on main\n@9bdb22f5887) is a runaway-loop **breaker/detector** only — `agent_call.py:144-197`\n`_runaway_guard_toolsets` computes a windowed distinct-ratio and raises `RunawayToolLoopError`\nbefore the repeated call executes, and stops advising `REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS` raises. Detection\nlanded; **elimination of the loop did not.** `completion.py:83` still documents the underlying\n\"~77% read_file re-read waste.\" So the guard now converts a slow budget-burn into a fast\nabort, but the ticket still cannot close through the gate — the author-facing outcome is\nunchanged. This bug tracks that residual (incomplete fix / regression of sunbittern's stated\ngoal); there is currently no open ticket for it.\n\n## Reproduction (2026-08-13, closing story `cinderlike-lucky-akitainu` 5e53-234f-5c65-477d)\n\nStory with 8 ACs, mostly codebase-verifiable, all provably met in-tree at origin/main\n`065af7c1639b954b045de95974654ba522ff4717` (independently verified: file LOC counts,\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:448-467`, `docs/architecture.md:327-332` + `:351`,\nGerrit 1751/1752/1753 merged commits reachable from HEAD). Two close attempts:\n\n- Run 1 (default budget): `completion-verifier ... hit step budget (request_limit=32\n  max_iterations=64)` in 105s, requests=32 tool_calls=43 — 3 unmet criteria, all\n  false-negatives (evidence present but not reached).\n- Run 2 (`REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS=128`, model `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`):\n  `aborted a runaway tool-call loop in 149.0s requests=47 tool_calls=57 distinct=45\n  max_consecutive_repeat=12 distinct_ratio_window=0.5\n  top_repeats=[{'signature': 'read_file:a0cce810', 'count': 13}]` — 2 unmet criteria; the\n  runaway guard tripped while re-reading one file (signature `read_file:a0cce810`, almost\n  certainly the 445-line `docs/architecture.md`) 13 times.\n\nDiagnostic (matches sunbittern's): raising the budget did NOT help — run 2 died on the\nrunaway guard at 47 requests, not on budget. The close ultimately required\n`rebar transition ... --force=<evidence>`, discarding the completion attestation — the exact\nanti-pattern sunbittern set out to prevent.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny ticket whose codebase-verifiable ACs force the verifier to consult a large file (e.g.\n`docs/architecture.md`) cannot close through the gate; the author must `--force`. This erodes\nthe completion gate as a safety mechanism across the project, not just for this one ticket.\n\n## Suspected mechanism (NOT verified end-to-end; for the owner to confirm)\n\nThe verifier agent re-issues byte-identical `read_file` calls on large files (paginated/\ntruncated reads it never fully consumes), wasting its budget until either the budget or the\nrunaway guard ends the run before all criteria are banked. The loop breaker prevents the\nbudget-burn but leaves the criteria unverified, so the verdict fail-closes.\n\n## Proposed directions (do NOT implement here — record only)\n\n- De-duplicate / cache file reads so an identical `read_file` returns cached content instead\n  of re-invoking the tool; and/or ensure large-file reads are consumed in full (or chunked\n  deterministically) so the agent does not re-request the same range.\n- Let the verifier bank partial per-criterion verdicts and treat a guard-abort as \"verify the\n  remainder on re-run\" rather than a whole-run fail-closed, so a complete ticket converges\n  across runs.\n- Consider capping per-file evidence reads or feeding large codebase evidence to the verifier\n  pre-summarized.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A ticket whose codebase-verifiable ACs require reading a large repo file (reproduce with\n      an akitainu-shaped fixture referencing `docs/architecture.md`) closes through the\n      completion gate WITHOUT `--force`, with no runaway-guard abort and no budget exhaustion.\n- [ ] The verifier no longer re-issues byte-identical `read_file`/`search_files` calls on the\n      same target within a run (assert distinct-call ratio stays healthy on the fixture trace).\n- [ ] Regression guard added so a future change that reintroduces the re-read loop fails a test\n      (not merely the runtime guard).","id":"3211-be4f-d4aa-4b5c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion verifier still loops on repeated file reads, blocking legitimate closes despite the runaway-guard fix (incomplete fix of brusque-tippable-sunbittern)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786680793409960001,"uuid":"294efa14-922a-4c68-8a05-e05775f25800"}